1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,100
The voltage swings all the time.

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:07,900
The peak is actually 325 V.

3
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:13,300
A heater warms with u², and u² is never negative.

4
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:18,900
Its average is exactly half the peak squared.

5
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,400
DC with the same heat is the RMS value.

6
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:25,400
Square root of a half: divide by √2.

7
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:30,900
325 V divided by 1.414 is 230 V. The RMS value!

8
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:37,400
On board, 440 V peaks at 622 V.

9
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:43,900
Insulation is stressed by the peak and by transients.

10
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:48,900
So next time you see 230 V, think 325.
